  "authoringNote": "Every pack rule applies to every case and only R10 has a not_applicable outcome, so the out-of-scope fact is reported by R01 alone and every other rule is still evaluated (matrix decision, question 3). No code is inferred or recommended and no payer action is represented. The case supplierStatus.status is the enum member unknown, so R01.scope_fact_unknown holds qualified by case.supplierStatus.status, naming no document. The current usable named supplier record, kept consistent with the case, states status unknown, so R01.supplier_record_value_unknown holds qualified by supplier.status and names that record. Both are missing outcomes for the authorization coordinator with scope_hold; no R01 conflict holds, because a disagreement needs a known value on both sides and the case value is unknown, and unknown never implies an exempt or non-exempt supplier. The finding is missing and its parent affectedDocuments is empty (the S reference is condition level only, C07). R01 cites the eight supplier and order item code facts, including the record's non-null status value unknown. Every other finding follows the supported packet, checked by hand: the final encounter (2026-08-26) and final signed order (2026-09-04) name practitioner identifier SYN-PRAC-0001, and the order is after the encounter and within the C01 bound 2027-02-26; the receipt references the order version and is recorded at 2026-09-05T18:40:00Z, after the C06 span 2026-09-03T10:00:00Z to 2026-09-05T12:00:00Z of the date-only order; the named supplier record is usable and hash-valid. R02 passes with six beneficiary citations (encounter, order, receipt), R03 passes with nine, R04 with six (status, date and practitioner identifier of each final document; null times supply no fact), R05 with four. R06 stays manual_review for the qualified clinical reviewer with R06.clinical_review and the five full /clinical/ pointers; it neither blocks nor satisfies readiness and draws no medical necessity conclusion. R07 passes citing the stated LCMP flag false; no ATP, specialty, home assessment or proof-of-delivery item is required. R08 and R09 pass. R10 is not_applicable with R10.pure_assessment. Quarantine and superseded lists are empty and clinicalReviewRequired is true. Parent affectedDocuments are empty: no held condition is restricted, unreadable or failed provenance (C07).",
